            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0557" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.52/458: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-10T00:00:00-04:00">May 10,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1317. Situation reported in Tangier’s 107, May 8, 7 p.m. is seriously disturbing.
                    Unless prompt measures are taken by Spanish Government <pb facs="0558" n="546"
                        xml:id="pg546"/> effectively to carry out agreement in regard to expulsion
                    of Germans, Department will be compelled to consider withdrawing its
                    authorization of petroleum loadings for Spain.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Tangier and Algiers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
